 {"id":"fabro-e6df","title":"gofib: add README with usage and flag reference","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T11:38:40.410Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T11:47:51.762Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA README.md at the repo root that documents the gofib CLI: what it is\n(Go CLI printing Fibonacci numbers), install/build via mise/just,\nusage, and the full flag reference.\n\n## Flag reference to cover\n\n- `-n <int>`: how many numbers to print (default 100, must be >= 1)\n- `-json`: JSON Lines output, one object per number (`{\"index\":<int>,\"fib\":\"<string>\"}`)\n- `-pretty`: aligned column output\n- `-version`: print version and exit\n\nUse the vocabulary from CONTEXT.md (text mode, JSON mode, count flag).\nShow real example invocations and their actual output — run the built\nbinary to capture it, do not invent output.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- README.md exists at the repo root\n- Examples match actual binary behavior\n- `just qualitygate` green","closedAt":"2026-08-24T11:47:51.762Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-4f3e","title":"gofib: add -start flag to begin printing at a given index","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T14:23:57.517Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T14:33:23.460Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-start <int>` flag: the first Fibonacci index to print. Default 0.\nCombines with `-n` (how many), `-json`, and `-pretty`.\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-start 10 -n 5` prints indices 10..14 in the active output mode\n  (text mode line format stays `<index>: <value>`).\n- Validation mirrors the `-n` contract: values < 0 exit non-zero with a\n  stderr error message.\n- `-start` must not change what `-n` counts (still the number of lines).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Flag parsed via the flag package; `Fib(n)` stays the only computation\n  (no inline recomputation — see CONTEXT.md).\n- Table-driven tests: default start, start+n combination, start with\n  -json and -pretty, negative start rejected.\n- README.md flag table gains the `-start` row; example invocation with\n  REAL output captured from the built binary (do not invent output).\n- `just qualitygate` green","closedAt":"2026-08-24T14:33:23.460Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-8208","title":"gofib: add -limit flag to cap output size safely","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T16:14:54.720Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T16:31:03.919Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-limit <int>` flag: hard cap on the LARGEST index gofib will print,\nindependent of `-start`/`-n`. Protects against accidental huge output\nwhen `-n` is large (e.g. `-n 100000` should still stop at the limit).\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-limit <int>`: do not print any index > limit. Default: no limit.\n- Combines with `-start` and `-n`: the effective output is the\n  intersection of all three (start <= index <= limit, at most -n lines).\n- Validation mirrors existing flags: values < 0 exit non-zero with a\n  stderr error message.\n- `-limit` smaller than `-start` produces empty output (zero lines),\n  NOT an error — document this in the README.\n- `-json` and `-pretty` combine as usual on the reduced set.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Flag parsed via the flag package; `Fib(n)` stays the only computation\n  (no inline recomputation — CONTEXT.md).\n- Table-driven tests: default (no limit), limit caps large -n, limit+start\n  intersection, limit < start gives empty output and exit 0, negative\n  limit rejected, limit with -json and -pretty.\n- README.md flag table gains the `-limit` row with a REAL example\n  invocation and its actual output (capture from the built binary, do not\n  invent output).\n- `just qualitygate` green","closedAt":"2026-08-24T16:31:03.919Z"}
-{"id":"fabro-cfb6","title":"gofib: add -seed flag for reproducible index selection","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T19:15:32.840Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T19:15:32.840Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-seed <int>` flag: print ONLY the Fibonacci number at a given index\n(one line) — a tiny lookup mode instead of a range, for spot-checks and\nscripting against specific indices.\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-seed i` prints exactly one entry for index `i` in the active output\n  mode: text mode `i: <value>`; JSON mode one object\n  `{\"index\":i,\"fib\":\"<string>\"}`; pretty mode single-row alignment.\n- `-seed` overrides the RANGE flags: with `-seed 10 -n 5 -start 2` only\n  index 10 prints (exactly one line). Document that precedence in the\n  README row.\n- `-version` keeps its top precedence (existing behavior, README pins\n  it).\n- Validation mirrors the other flags: values < 0 exit non-zero with a\n  stderr error. `-seed 0` behaves like `-start 0`: treated as unset\n  (sentinel), so plain `gofib` output stays unchanged.\n- `Fib(n)` stays the only computation — no inline recomputation\n  (CONTEXT.md).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Table-driven tests: single index via -seed; -seed overrides -n/-start\n  (and -limit); -seed 0 sentinel; -seed with -json and -pretty;\n  negative rejected; -version still wins.\n- README.md flag table gains the `-seed` row with a REAL example\n  invocation and its actual output (capture from the built binary, do\n  not invent output); the precedence note lives in that row.\n- `just qualitygate` green"}
+{"id":"fabro-cfb6","title":"gofib: add -seed flag for reproducible index selection","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T19:15:32.840Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T22:20:28.564Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-seed <int>` flag: print ONLY the Fibonacci number at a given index\n(one line) — a tiny lookup mode instead of a range, for spot-checks and\nscripting against specific indices.\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-seed i` prints exactly one entry for index `i` in the active output\n  mode: text mode `i: <value>`; JSON mode one object\n  `{\"index\":i,\"fib\":\"<string>\"}`; pretty mode single-row alignment.\n- `-seed` overrides the RANGE flags: with `-seed 10 -n 5 -start 2` only\n  index 10 prints (exactly one line). Document that precedence in the\n  README row.\n- `-version` keeps its top precedence (existing behavior, README pins\n  it).\n- Validation mirrors the other flags: values < 0 exit non-zero with a\n  stderr error. `-seed 0` behaves like `-start 0`: treated as unset\n  (sentinel), so plain `gofib` output stays unchanged.\n- `Fib(n)` stays the only computation — no inline recomputation\n  (CONTEXT.md).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Table-driven tests: single index via -seed; -seed overrides -n/-start\n  (and -limit); -seed 0 sentinel; -seed with -json and -pretty;\n  negative rejected; -version still wins.\n- README.md flag table gains the `-seed` row with a REAL example\n  invocation and its actual output (capture from the built binary, do\n  not invent output); the precedence note lives in that row.\n- `just qualitygate` green"}
 {"id":"fabro-d920","title":"gofib: add -format flag for compact table output","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T22:19:17.606Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T22:19:17.606Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-format <mode>` flag selecting the OUTPUT STYLE globally, unifying\nthe text/json/pretty matrix: `text` (default), `json`, `pretty`, and a\nnew compact `table` mode (no leading index column, values only, one\nper line).\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-format text|json|pretty|table` — invalid values exit non-zero with\n  a stderr error listing valid modes.\n- `-json` and `-pretty` remain as SHORTCUTS: `-json` == `-format json`,\n  `-pretty` == `-format pretty`. If BOTH a shortcut and `-format` are\n  given and they conflict (e.g. `-pretty -format json`), exit non-zero\n  with a clear error — no silent precedence.\n- `table` mode: values only, one per line (aligned, right-justified to\n  the widest value). Composes with `-start`/`-n`/`-limit` as usual.\n- `-version` still wins over everything.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Flag via the flag package; existing behavior for `-json`/`-pretty`\n  UNCHANGED (regression tests pin them).\n- Table-driven tests: each mode, shortcut==format equivalence, conflict\n  rejection, invalid mode rejection, table+start/n/limit combos.\n- README flag table gains the `-format` row with a REAL example per\n  mode (capture from the built binary; do not invent output).\n- `just qualitygate` green"}
